## Summary

Fixed Helios When's `/e/<id>` page hanging at "Looking…" for events the calendar model hasn't loaded (the model loads only events with a `start`, e.g. `/e/grpykdcGhNGQEC`, LARP Junior League).

- Cause: `eventRoute` (`web/when/app.js`) calls `fetchEvent` (alias lookup into the same `byId`), and only re-rendered when it found the event, so a miss never left "Looking…".
- Fix: `fetchEvent(id).then(render)` always re-renders; the second pass sees the id in `fetched` and shows the existing "That event not found" page.
- Left out: making undated events actually viewable in When (would need loading them separately); they now show "not found" rather than hanging.
- Removed the TODO.md item. Merged main cleanly; `go vet ./...` passes; no tests cover this route, and it was not exercised in a browser.

